{
 "id": "k8s-cri-pod-sandboxes",
 "version": 2,
 "logsource": {
  "product": "kubernetes",
  "service": "cri"
 },
 "fidelity": "synthetic",
 "represents": "About 3 hours of pod-sandbox starts across the 9 nodes of the same staging cluster as the node runtime sensor reports them: Deployment and CoreDNS replicas from rollouts, restarts and reschedules, DaemonSet node agents, StatefulSet replicas, Actions Runner Controller ephemeral CI runner pods, Helm hook and manual Job pods, and Deployment sandboxes recreated after a node reboot (attempt 1). Every draw is a new pod with its own name and uid, so a (uid, attempt) pair occurs once. The schedule-bound pods (CronJob runs, the kubeadm static pods) are in k8s-cri-cronjob-static-pods, written once each. Template weights set which pod kinds appear and roughly how often relative to each other, not production rates; treat hits and rate_per_10k as presence indicators.",
 "provenance": "synthetic; shapes from `crictl pods -o json` (CRI PodSandbox: id, metadata {name, uid, namespace, attempt}, state, createdAt as nanoseconds since the epoch, labels incl. io.kubernetes.pod.*, annotations incl. kubernetes.io/config.seen and config.source) as detections/k8s/cri-pod-sensor.sh records it; Job pod labels per the batch/v1 Job controller (batch.kubernetes.io/job-name, controller-uid, legacy job-name); ARC runner labels per gha-runner-scale-set 0.9. A sandbox's annotations are the pod's own plus the kubelet's kubernetes.io/config.* (the Job controller tracks pods with a finalizer, not a pod annotation); pod names are the owner's name plus 5 characters of k8s.io/apimachinery's rand alphabet, uids are random per draw, so no two draws are the same pod; a sandbox is re-created for an existing pod only as attempt N+1. Sandbox start times are drawn from the window, not ordered; names are fictional, addresses RFC1918.",
 "adjacent_to": [
  "T1053.007/k8s_cri_job_pod.yml (Helm hook and manual Job pods match; CI runner pods do not)",
  "T1543.005/k8s_cri_static_pod_start.yml (no static pods here: see k8s-cri-cronjob-static-pods)"
 ],
